__pycache__/
*.pyc
# BUILD OUTPUT THAT ALSO HAS TO BE IGNORED *AT THE ROOT*, not just nested
# (measured 2026-09-01, and the reason `eas build` was impossible to run).
#
# Both paths are already ignored by their own nested .gitignore
# (surfaces/app/.gitignore ':/android', surfaces/desktop/.gitignore 'release/')
# and neither holds a single TRACKED file - so for git these two lines are a
# no-op and exist purely as documentation. They are here because eas-cli's
# archiver does NOT reliably apply nested .gitignore files when it copies the
# project: `surfaces/app/dist-desktop/` (a ROOT rule) was correctly excluded
# from the upload while `surfaces/app/android/` and `surfaces/desktop/release/`
# (NESTED rules) were both copied in whole. That put 5.4 GB of pure build
# output - android/app/build 1.3 GB + 3.9 GB of stale HelmDeck-Setup-*.exe -
# into a 4.2 GB tarball, and EAS hard-rejects any archive above 2.0 GB
# ("Project archive is too big"), so every iOS build died at upload.
#
# The fix is deliberately NOT a .easignore, even though eas-cli's own error
# message recommends one: vcs/local.js documents "if .easignore exists,
# .gitignore files are not used", so adding one would silently drop EVERY
# secret rule below (.env, *.p8, daemon/users.json, daemon/helmdeck.db,
# .attachments/) and upload them to EAS. Same
# allowlist-vs-denylist trap electron-builder.yml already records.
surfaces/app/android/
surfaces/desktop/release/
# GENERIC log net (2026-08-24 data-hygiene audit): every log is runtime
# output, wherever a future feature drops one - the named entries further
# down predate this rule and stay as documentation of what writes where.
# Verified before adding: zero tracked *.log/*.err existed.
*.log
*.err
daemon/recordings/
.idea/
*.keystore
push.env

# Local expo modules ARE tracked (surfaces/app/modules/glasses is real source), but a
# native build drops gradle output inside them - first seen 2026-08-21, when
# assembleRelease left surfaces/app/modules/glasses/android/build/ as ~700 untracked
# files. Ignore the output, keep the source.
surfaces/app/modules/*/android/build/
daemon/tracks.json
daemon/settings.json
daemon/relay_feed.json
daemon/plane_links.json
daemon/plane_credentials.txt
daemon/events.jsonl
daemon/users.json
daemon/users.json.tmp
daemon/processes.json
daemon/asc_review_watch.json
# config-consolidation phase 7 (2026-09-03): daemon/ runtime bookkeeping
# (sessions.json, copilot_sessions.json, driver_pids.json, ...) and durable
# content a feature produces about itself (henry_memory/, voice_cache/,
# models_stt/, copilot_runs/) both moved from loose flat files into these two
# folders (spine/registry/db.py's relocator, daemon/paths.py's STATE_SUBDIR/
# CONTENT_SUBDIR). Blanket rules replace the individual flat-file entries
# above (sessions.json, copilot_sessions.json, copilot_models.json,
# voice_cache/ used to be named here one by one) - nothing tracked lives in
# either folder. board_directives.json is the one exception that stays flat
# and tracked (real repo data, see db.py's _RELOCATE_STATE comment).
daemon/state/
daemon/content/
# Scratch space for a turn's throwaway artifacts (fixtures, downloaded release
# assets staged for re-upload, generated notes). Added 2026-09-08 after a
# baseline snapshot swept two throwaway test scripts into a commit: anything
# under daemon/ is machine-local by the rule above, but tmp/ had no entry, so
# `git add -A` picked it up. Nothing here is ever meant to be tracked.
daemon/tmp/
# GxP signing keys (spine/auth/signkeys.py): per-user GPG keyrings whose
# passphrase is the user's password. Private keys are secrets like users.json
# above; the PUBLIC keys an auditor needs are exported per signature, and even
# those stay out of git - they belong to an installation, not the source.
daemon/signkeys/
daemon/checkpoints/
daemon/swarmdeck.db
daemon/helmdeck.db
daemon/*.imported
daemon/*.imported.*
daemon/**/*.imported
daemon/tracks.json.imported
# events.jsonl sync/import runtime markers - a *.imported (no numbered
# suffix) is already covered above; *.imported.<n> and *.synced are the
# same class of daemon-regenerated marker and were missing (surfaced by a
# throwaway verification daemon run leaving events.jsonl.imported.2 /
# events.jsonl.synced as untracked noise).
daemon/*.synced
daemon/**/*.synced
# ad-hoc one-off diagnostic scripts left by a session with direct hands on
# the live tree (Henry) - disposable scratch, never source. Generalized
# twice: root-level _*.py, and _henry*/_inspect* anywhere (he drops them
# next to whatever he is inspecting, measured 2026-08-24 in ops/tools/).
/_*.py
**/_henry*.py
**/_inspect*.py
.loop/
daemon/copilot_log.json
daemon/copilot_stats.json
daemon/driver_pids.json
daemon/recorder_pids.json
