# early APK; the whole dir is machine-local now.
daemon/nightshift/
daemon/restart_stdout.log
daemon/restart_stderr.log
daemon/daemon.out.log
surfaces/app/dist-desktop/
surfaces/app/web_dev.log
# tsc emit output for the zero-dependency self-tests (src/kernel/__selftest__.ts,
# src/kernel/__caps_selftest__.ts) - compiled JS, not source.
surfaces/app/.kernel-out/
surfaces/app/.capstest-out/
surfaces/app/.hubtest-out/
surfaces/app/.ui-out/
# screenshots + dev-server logs from the e2e_* UI judgements (ops/tests/e2e_*.py)
.verify/
daemon/swarmdeck.db-wal
daemon/swarmdeck.db-shm
daemon/helmdeck.db-wal
daemon/helmdeck.db-shm
backups/
# NOT an accident (owner decision 2026-08-16, "you work local so just don't
# publish docs"): already-tracked docs STAY tracked so card worktrees see them;
# this only keeps NEW docs out of git by default. The public mirror strips
# the whole tree - see the private-path check in ops/deploy/publish_source.sh.
# `ops/docs/**` (contents) instead of bare `docs` (the dir) since the root-
# minimization sweep: an ignored DIRECTORY cannot have children re-included,
# and ops/docs/backlog/ - the card queue, moved here 2026-08-24 - MUST track new
# cards or the dispatch workflow silently loses them. Everything else under
# ops/docs/ behaves exactly as before.
ops/docs/**
!ops/docs/backlog/
!ops/docs/backlog/**
# the re-include above overrides the global __pycache__/ rule for anything
# under backlog (later pattern wins) - a card's judge script run drops caches
ops/docs/backlog/**/__pycache__/

# local credentials - never commit
# App Store Connect API key. Apple serves the .p8 exactly ONCE - there is no
# re-download - and it can mint iOS signing certificates, so treat it like the
# Android keystore. ops/deploy/ios_credentials.sh additionally REFUSES to run when
# the key lives anywhere under this repo; this line is only the second net.
*.p8
daemon/certs/
.env
*.env
!.env.example
google-services.json
fcm_service_account.json
daemon/models_cache.json
daemon/pm/
ops/tests/banner_offline.png

# UI-judging screenshots (regenerate with ops/tests/uifix_shoot.py)
ops/tests/_shots/

# chat attachments the owner uploads (phone screenshots of his own board, etc).
# Runtime user data, exactly like daemon/recordings/ and daemon/checkpoints/ -
# electron-builder.yml already refuses to ship .attachments/** for the same
# reason. Ignoring it protects only the FUTURE: five of these were committed
# before this line existed and are still reachable in history, which is what
# ops/deploy/publish_source.sh's privacy check is there to catch before a push
# makes them public.
.attachments/
daemon/.attachments/
daemon/.copilot_attachments/

# Henry's durable memory (owner decree 2026-08-30, "Kompaktieren und ins
# Speicher") used to live at daemon/henry_memory/ and was ignored here for
# the same privacy reason as the two blocks above - it is the OWNER'S OWN
# conversation distilled. Removed 2026-09-11 (henry-memory-file-authority
# follow-up): memory has no filesystem surface at all anymore, the db
# (daemon/helmdeck.db, already ignored) is the only store, and a full note
# is read via ops/tools/henry_memory_get.py - nothing is ever written to
# this path again, so there is no directory left to ignore.

# deploy artifacts (generated by ops/deploy/ship.sh): the emulator smoke
# screenshot - machine-local, regenerated each ship. (The native fingerprint
# itself moved to a git ref, refs/helmdeck/last-native-fp - that's exactly
# the kind of file that broke across worktrees, so it isn't one anymore.)
ops/deploy/last_apk_smoke.png
# ops/deploy/asc_guide.py's screenshot of App Store Connect: regenerated on every
# `shot`, and once logged in it shows the owner's Apple ID and app list.
# (shots/ lives under ops/docs/ since the root-minimization sweep - ops/docs/ is also
# what the public mirror filters, closing the board-screenshot gap.)
ops/docs/shots/asc.png
# same reason: ops/deploy/meta_wearables_guide.py's screenshot shows the owner's
# Meta org/project details once logged in.
ops/docs/shots/meta_wearables.png
daemon/daemon.pid
surfaces/desktop/_probe_setup.js
surfaces/desktop/python/
copilot_runs/
# ops/harness/.versions: every /harness write archives the file it replaced so a bad
# edit is revertable. Machine-local undo history, not shipped policy - the
# CURRENT ops/harness/agents/*.md and ops/harness/settings/*.json are what's tracked.
ops/harness/.versions/

# surfaces/glasses/worker/public is GENERATED by ops/deploy/push_glance.sh from the three
