# Scratch file for `git commit -F`, which is how a multi-line commit message
# gets written here (a shell here-string is flattened by the rtk hook into
# pathspecs). Ignored because `git add -A` swept one into a commit, 2026-08-29.
.git-commit-msg.tmp

# Scratch clone a ship/publish step makes at repo root when it mirrors to the
# public MAS-CI remote (helmdeck-mas-ci) - found sitting at root, 449MB, quiet
# (2026-09-13), not made by any script under a name this repo owns, so left in
# place rather than deleted (CLAUDE.md: look at the target before deleting).
# Ignored so the build loop's clean-tree check stops flagging someone else's
# scratch directory as unstaged work. Globbed (not a fixed name) because the
# next run showed up as .publish-tmp-masci/ - same source, different suffix.
.publish-tmp-mas*/

